        "GXO Logistics 与 Agility Robotics 10 月 26 日宣布，把双方多年期的人形机器人合作从佐治亚州 Flowery Branch 单一站点扩展至北卡罗来纳州斯泰茨维尔与田纳西州黎巴嫩两个美国仓，新站点预计 2027 年初开始安装，初期部署 Digit 4，待 Digit 5 商用后迁移。合作沿革：2023 年底在 Flowery Branch 做概念验证，2024 年 6 月签署多年期“机器人即服务”（RaaS）协议——这是业内首个在真实运营环境中部署人形机器人的商业协议，也是首个人形机器人 RaaS 协议；截至宣布时，Digit 在该站点已搬运超过 10 万个周转箱（任务是把周转箱从 AMR 搬上传送带，与既有传送带自动化协同而非取代），跨客户累计真实运行超过 6.5 万小时，Tech Times 引用的在岗准确率约 98%。下一代硬件是此次扩容的关键变量：Digit 5 于 2026 年 9 月 15 日发布，运行/充电比由 Digit 4 的约 2:1（30 分钟运行 + 15 分钟充电）提升到 10:1（90 分钟运行 + 9 分钟充电），厂家称可实现每天 20 小时以上有效作业；机身 5 英尺 11 英寸、重 284 磅，负载 50 磅（约提升 40%）、最大触及 7.2 英尺，腿部改用自研摆线针轮致动器，末端支持 ISO 标准法兰快换夹爪，并成为首个搭载 NVIDIA IGX Thor 工业 AI 计算与 Halos 功能安全框架的平台。产能与订单：Agility 位于俄勒冈州塞勒姆的 RoboFab 工厂（7 万平方英尺）设计年产能最高 1 万台；公司披露 Digit 5 已获超过 3 亿美元（约 2.25 亿英镑）的多年承诺订单，但同时说明这是随时间实现的潜在价值、受合同里程碑与产品规格约束，并非当期收入，另有 30 余家潜在客户在商业洽谈中，AGCO 已于 10 月 20 日宣布 2027 年在堪萨斯州 Hesston 工厂试点。必须标注的局限：双方未披露本次扩容的合同金额、机器人台数与新站点吞吐目标，因此“人形机器人替代了多少人力”在外部仍不可验证；10 万个周转箱、6.5 万小时与 98% 准确率均为公司自行发布的数据，未经独立审计；Digit 5 早期客户交付预计在 2027 年上半年、全面可用目标为 2027 年底，即这批订单对应的机型距全面上市还有一年以上。",
        "GXO Logistics and Agility Robotics announced on 26 October that they are extending their multi-year humanoid partnership beyond the single Flowery Branch, Georgia site to two more US warehouses, in Statesville, North Carolina and Lebanon, Tennessee, with installations expected to begin in early 2027 running Digit 4 before migrating to Digit 5 once it is commercially available. The partnership began with a proof of concept at Flowery Branch in late 2023 and converted in June 2024 into a multi-year robots-as-a-service agreement — the industry’s first commercial deployment of humanoids in live operations and the first RaaS deal for a humanoid. As of the announcement, Digit has moved more than 100,000 totes at that site (lifting totes from autonomous mobile robots onto conveyors, working alongside existing conveyor automation rather than replacing it), with more than 65,000 cumulative real-world operating hours across customer deployments and on-task accuracy of about 98% per Tech Times. Next-generation hardware is the key variable: Digit 5, unveiled on 15 September 2026, lifts the run-to-charge ratio from roughly 2:1 on Digit 4 (30 minutes running, 15 minutes charging) to 10:1 (90 minutes running, 9 minutes charging), which the company says enables more than 20 productive hours a day. It stands 5 feet 11 inches and weighs 284 pounds, carries 50 pounds (about 40% more) to a 7.2-foot maximum reach, uses proprietary cycloidal actuators in rebuilt legs, accepts swappable end effectors on ISO-standard mounting flanges, and is the first Agility platform built on NVIDIA IGX Thor industrial AI compute with the Halos functional safety framework. On capacity and orders, Agility’s 70,000 sq ft RoboFab plant in Salem, Oregon is designed for up to 10,000 robots a year, and the company has disclosed more than $300m (about £225m) in committed multi-year orders for Digit 5 — while stating this is potential value to be realised over time, subject to contractual milestones and specifications and not current-period revenue — alongside more than 30 prospective customers in active commercial discussions and an AGCO pilot announced on 20 October for its Hesston, Kansas plant in 2027. Limits that must be stated: neither company disclosed the contract value, the number of robots, or throughput targets for the new sites, so how much human labour the humanoids replace remains unverifiable from outside; the 100,000 totes, 65,000 hours and 98% accuracy are company-published figures that have not been independently audited; and early customer access to Digit 5 is expected in the first half of 2027 with general availability targeted for end-2027, meaning the robot those orders are for is more than a year from full commercial sale.",
