        "2026 年 CeMAT ASIA 于 11 月 3—6 日在上海举行（以下为展前预告，非已发生事实）。西门子官方博客公布其在展会上的布局：以 Digital Enterprise 把规划、工程、自动化与仓储运营用连续数字主线串起来，现场演示由 SIMOVE 与 Fleet Manager 编排的人形机器人与 AMR 自主物料流，并展示 Mobile Walker、Engineering Copilot TIA、工程与预测性维护智能体，以及 Plant Simulation 与 MCD 等运营软件，另设 Express 2.0 跨境电商解决方案中心与 XCargo 现场演示。库卡移动机器人以“开天 KAI”工业 AI 平台切入仓储场景，主打“软件底座 + 硬件产品 + 行业方案”全栈：KMP L 系列潜伏顶升式移动机器人、一站式托盘搬运解决方案与 KUKA.AMR 软件 3.0 分别指向安全边界、场景效率与系统协同，现场将演示“收货入库—物料转运—高位存储—分拣出库”的多系统端到端闭环。极智嘉则深化托盘、货箱与无人拣货三条线：RoboShuttle Hyper 货箱到人攀爬机器人在本届全球首秀并配合无人拣选工作站实景演绎；托盘侧以 SkyCube 四向穿梭车（上存下拣构型）与 RoboPallet 托盘大小车两条互补路线覆盖高、中流量场景，其中 RoboPallet 面向净高 13 米以下、SKU 多、吞吐适中的传统人工叉车仓与租赁仓，可复用现有横梁货架、兼容“田”字与“川”字托盘及木托盘而无需额外母托盘，最快 1 个月交付，预计 2027 年 1 月进入量产并推向市场。三家厂商的展览主题指向同一件事：行业竞争点正从“单机参数”转向调度、交管与异常处理能否同步跟上，以及 WMS/WCS/MES/ERP 之间能否真正咬合。须标注：上述均为厂商展前公开信息，量产时间等为计划值，尚无第三方验证的实际交付数据。",
        "CeMAT ASIA 2026 runs in Shanghai from 3 to 6 November; the following is a pre-show preview rather than an account of what has already happened. Siemens’ official blog sets out its presence: a Digital Enterprise digital thread linking planning, engineering, automation and warehouse operations, with an on-site demonstration of autonomous material flow in which humanoid robots and AMRs are orchestrated by SIMOVE and Fleet Manager, plus Mobile Walker, Engineering Copilot TIA, engineering and predictive-maintenance agents, and operations software including Plant Simulation and MCD; an Express 2.0 cross-border e-commerce solution centre and an XCargo demonstration are also planned. KUKA mobile robots bring their “Kaitian KAI” industrial AI platform to warehouse scenarios under a full-stack software-base, hardware-product, industry-solution structure: the KMP L-series low-profile lifting AMR, a one-stop pallet-handling solution and KUKA.AMR software 3.0 address safety boundaries, scene efficiency and system coordination respectively, with a live end-to-end loop covering receiving, material transfer, high-bay storage and sortation. Geek+ is deepening three lines — pallet, tote and unmanned picking. RoboShuttle Hyper, a tote-to-person climbing robot, makes its global debut with a live unmanned picking workstation; on the pallet side, SkyCube four-way shuttles (store-above, pick-below configuration) and the RoboPallet truck-and-cart system cover high and medium throughput respectively, with RoboPallet aimed at conventional forklift and leased warehouses under 13 metres clear height with many SKUs and moderate throughput, able to reuse existing beam racking, accept “tian” and “chuan” pattern pallets and wooden pallets without extra mother pallets, deliverable in as little as one month, with mass production and market launch planned for January 2027. All three point the same way: competition is shifting from single-machine specifications to whether dispatch, traffic management and exception handling keep pace, and whether WMS, WCS, MES and ERP can actually interlock. Caveat: this is vendor pre-show information; dates such as the mass-production timeline are plans with no third-party-verified delivery data yet.",
